                <pb facs="1035" n="939" sameAs="frus:frus1926v02/pg939"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.162/74: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Salvador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Engert</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-24T13:00:00-06:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 24, 1926—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>68. Speaker of the National Assembly has just informed me that the Deputies are
                    opposed to ratification of the treaty before the United States Senate ratifies
                    it. As the Assembly adjourns in one week till February prompt action
                    necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Engert</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
